  "turns": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild a three-story, single-bay planar concrete frame with span 6 m, three story heights of 3.3 m and both bases fixed. The completed appendix specifies C30 (E=30000 MPa, nu=0.2, G=12500 MPa, density=2500 kg/m^3), 500x500 mm columns C1 and 300x600 mm beams B1. D applies downward full-span line loads of 12, 10 and 8 kN/m to floors 1, 2 and 3. W+ applies global +X forces of 10, 15 and 20 kN at the right node of floors 1, 2 and 3. W- is a separate case with the same positions and exactly opposite forces. Analyze precisely these three linear combinations: C0=D; C+=D+W+; C-=D+W-. Run first-order linear elastic Euler-Bernoulli analysis in OpenSees, self weight off. For each combination separately, report signed ux at both column lines on all three floors, all six signed story displacement differences ux(upper)-ux(lower), Fx/Fz/My at both bases and M2 at both ends of both first-story columns. Preserve the original signs and the distinct case and combination labels.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
        "output-requests.json",
        "analysis-conventions.txt"
      ],
      "unresolvedFields": [],
      "expectedQuestions": []
    }
  ],
